    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nguyên âm · The last compound vowels",
     "texto": [
      "These vowels are used in very few words, so instead of long exercises we practise with real words.",
      "**uê**: «weh»: **Huế** ≈ «hweh».",
      "**ưu**: ư + u: **cứu** (to help), **bưu điện** (post office).",
      "**ươu**: ư + ơ + u: **rượu** (alcohol, liquor).",
      "**Exceptions**: **oe** (khỏe), **uya** (khuya), **uyu** (khuỷu), **uây** (khuấy) and **ưi** (gửi).",
      "You already know the whole Vietnamese alphabet! From here on, the best practice is to review the conversations and speak as much as you can."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
